B 0xB042 THE TARGET THAT CLOSES THE STRETCH AND OPENS THE BONUS STAGE
B 0xB042 Five stages (1, 2, 3, 4 and 7) have a distance written into them at which
B 0xB042 a target appears: it is not one of the usual objects, but three loose
B 0xB042 bytes at 0xE1C1..0xE1C3 (type, row and column) that move with the
B 0xB042 scroll. If the ship passes over it, with a margin of 0x10 in both
B 0xB042 directions, everything on screen blows up, the scroll stops at a limit of
B 0xB042 the stage's own, the script line is erased and sound 0xCD plays.
B 0xB042 AND IT IS ALSO THE DOOR TO THE BONUS STAGES. 0xB130 is the ONLY thing in
B 0xB042 the 128 KB that makes 0xE1C0 non-zero, and p01:0x6D66, 0x6DA7, 0x6E15 and
B 0xB042 0x6F19 (the finals of stages 2, 3, 4 and 7) look at exactly that byte:
B 0xB042 with the screen stopped they jump to stages 9, 10, 11 and 12, and
B 0xB042 otherwise they carry on with their normal script. So touching the target
B 0xB042 at the end of those four stages is what opens the interlude. The target
B 0xB042 of stage 1 leads to none.
